摘要中的主要功能必须被所选片段支持。优先把改变用途含义的条件写进摘要，不能只藏在limitations。遇到“阶段1骨架”“cloud provider待实现”“匿名thread后续实现”等，摘要明确当前仅本地草稿/审批落盘，不说已实现匿名网络或云端发布。Codex/模型登录适配归coding-development；Oopz等语音房的对话连接归communication-integrations。自述兼容或性能用“作者称/README注明”，不冒充本次验证。
格式示例（仅结构，不是来源事实）：evidence:[{"paragraph_id":"p3s1","fact":"该片段支持的中文转述"}]。请从本次真实输入挑选编号。","role":"system"},{"content":"{"metadata":{"description":"Gitea/Forgejo toolkit for DeepSeek Harness: issues, PRs, CI, releases, operations","id":"gh:1352549172","install_available":true,"language":"JavaScript","name":"dsh-gitea","slug":"GooDAnDReaDY/dsh-gitea","topics":["deepseek-harness","dsh","dsh-plugin"]},"paragraphs":[{"id":"p1s1","text":"Gitea/Forgejo toolkit for DeepSeek Harness: issues, PRs, CI, releases, operations"},{"id":"p2s1","text":"# 📦 @goodandready/dsh-gitea"},{"id":"p3s1","text":"Enterprise Gitea & Forgejo Integration Suite for DeepSeek Harness"},{"id":"p4s1","text":"🇬🇧 English •\n🇷🇺 Русский •\n🇨🇳 中文说明"},{"id":"p5s1","text":"⭐ If you like this plugin, please star it on GitHub — it shows me that the plugin is useful to you a"},{"id":"p5s2","text":"nd motivates me to keep developing it."},{"id":"p6s1","text":"🐛 If you find a bug or would like to request a feature, open a GitHub issue in any language — I will"},{"id":"p6s2","text":" review your proposal and implement useful suggestions in a future plugin version."},{"id":"p7s1","text":"### 🌟 What's New in v0.7.6\n- **One-Click Auto-Updater**: Check npm and upgrade directly in the DSH s"},{"id":"p7s2","text":"ettings card.\n- **Composition Services**: Exposes `dshGitea` (task provisioning) and `giteaEvents` ("},{"id":"p7s3","text":"safe telemetry bridge for `@goodandready/dsh-pulse`).\n- **Security & Hygiene**: Loopback and origin-"},{"id":"p7s4","text":"hardened HTTP write guards (`lib/http-guard.js`), sanitized GitHub release export pipeline (`publish"},{"id":"p7s5","text":".sh`).\n- **Performance & Caching**: Cache invalidation on git mutations and modularized `lib/tool-de"},{"id":"p7s6","text":"- **Performance & Caching**: Cache invalidation on git mutations and modularized `lib/tool-defs.js`."},{"id":"p8s1","text":"### 🌟 What's New in v0.7.5\n- **Canonical English Server & Agent Tool Outputs**: All tool responses, "},{"id":"p8s2","text":"verification details, and error messages conform strictly to `dsh-plugin-authoring` canonical Englis"},{"id":"p8s3","text":"h standard.\n- **Clean Package Boundaries**: Standalone issue form templates are safely organized in "},{"id":"p8s4","text":"`assets/issue-templates/`; internal development specs (`docs/superpowers/`, `.gitea/`) are strictly "},{"id":"p8s5","text":"excluded from npm packages.\n- **Automated Compliance Quality Gate**: Permanent test coverage enforci"},{"id":"p8s6","text":"ng 0 Cyrillic characters across `lib/` and strict package file boundary audits."},{"id":"p9s1","text":"## ⚡ Overview & Problem Solved"},{"id":"p10s1","text":"When autonomous AI coding agents perform complex multi-step development in DeepSeek Harness, they re"},{"id":"p10s2","text":"quire seamless access to issue trackers, pull request review workflows, branch creation, and isolate"},{"id":"p10s3","text":"d workspace worktrees without risking repository corruption or leaking credentials into chat logs."},{"id":"p11s1","text":"**`@goodandready/dsh-gitea`** bridges DeepSeek Harness to self-hosted **Gitea** and **Forgejo** inst"},{"id":"p11s2","text":"ances. It equips agents with a complete suite of 20+ structured tools, registers a live **Git Status"},{"id":"p11s3","text":" Chip** directly in the Web UI chat header, and enforces safety rails (`confirm: true` merge guards "},{"id":"p11s4","text":"and dedicated write wrappers)."},{"id":"p12s1","text":"## 🏗️ Architecture"},{"id":"p13s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p14s1","text":"## ✨ Full Feature Breakdown"},{"id":"p15s1","text":"### 1. 20+ Agent Tools Suite"},{"id":"p16s1","text":"All tools infer `owner` and `repo` automatically from the active workspace's `git remote get-url ori"},{"id":"p16s2","text":"gin` when omitted by the agent."},{"id":"p17s1","text":"| Tool Name | Scope | Description | Safety Requirements |\n|:---|:---|:---|:---|\n| `gitea_labels` | L"},{"id":"p17s2","text":"abels | Consolidated label facade: `list`, `create`, `delete`, `set` | - |\n| `gitea_milestones` | Mi"},{"id":"p17s3","text":"lestones | Consolidated milestone facade: `list`, `create`, `update`, `delete` | ⚠️ Delete requires "},{"id":"p17s4","text":"`confirm: true` |\n| `gitea_releases` | Releases | Consolidated release facade: `list`, `create`, `up"},{"id":"p17s5","text":"date`, `delete`, `plan`, `notes` | ⚠️ Delete requires `confirm: true` |\n| `gitea_ci` | CI / Actions "},{"id":"p17s6","text":"| Consolidated CI facade: `status`, `jobs`, `rerun`, `explain` | ⚠️ Rerun requires `confirm: true` |"},{"id":"p17s7","text":"\n| `gitea_branches` | Branches | Consolidated branch facade: `list`, `create`, `delete` | ⚠️ Delete "},{"id":"p17s8","text":"requires `confirm: true` |\n| `gitea_tags` | Tags | Consolidated tag facade: `list`, `create`, `delet"},{"id":"p17s9","text":"e` | ⚠️ Delete requires `confirm: true` |\n| `gitea_webhooks` | Webhooks | Consolidated webhook facad"},{"id":"p17s10","text":"e: `list`, `create`, `delete` | ⚠️ Delete requires `confirm: true` |\n| `gitea_org` | Org & Teams | C"},{"id":"p17s11","text":"onsolidated organization facade: `list`, `repos`, `members`, `teams`, `create_repo` | - |\n| `gitea_w"},{"id":"p17s12","text":"iki` | Wiki | Consolidated wiki facade: `list`, `get` | - |\n| `gitea_issue_create` | Issues | Create"},{"id":"p17s13","text":"s a new issue with title, body, labels, and assignees | - |\n| `gitea_issue_list` | Issues | Lists is"},{"id":"p17s14","text":"sues with state (`open`/`closed`), milestone, and label filters | - |\n| `gitea_issue_get` | Issues |"},{"id":"p17s15","text":" Fetches detailed issue data by issue index | - |\n| `gitea_issue_comment`| Issues | Posts comments, "},{"id":"p17s16","text":"progress updates, and code reviews | - |\n| `gitea_issue_comments`| Issues | Lists comments for an is"},{"id":"p17s17","text":"sue (annotated with `mine: true/false`) | - |\n| `gitea_issue_comment_delete`| Issues | Deletes own i"},{"id":"p17s18","text":"ssue comment (safe dry-run preview by default; only current token user comments can be deleted) | ⚠️"},{"id":"p17s19","text":" Requires `confirm: true` |\n| `gitea_issue_update` | Issues | Updates issue title, body, or status |"},{"id":"p17s20","text":" - |\n| `gitea_issue_close`  | Issues | Closes an issue | - |\n[该节后续省略]"},{"id":"p18s1","text":"### 2. Per-branch PR templates"},{"id":"p19s1","text":"When creating a PR via issue-flow without an explicit body, the plugin fills a template by branch ty"},{"id":"p19s2","text":"pe: `feat/`, `fix/`, `docs/`, `chore/`, `refactor/`."},{"id":"p20s1","text":"### 3. Live Git Status Chip & Topological Commit Graph"},{"id":"p21s1","text":"The client component injects a real-time Git Status Chip into the DSH Web UI chat header:\n* **Active"},{"id":"p21s2","text":" Repository & Branch**: Displays current branch name (e.g., `feature/issue-42-auth`).\n* **Tree Clean"},{"id":"p21s3","text":"liness**: Color-coded badges indicating clean vs dirty working trees and modified files count.\n* **A"},{"id":"p21s4","text":"head/Behind Sync Badges**: Real-time sync indicator (`↑ahead`, `↓behind`) relative to upstream or `o"},{"id":"p21s5","text":"rigin/<branch>`.\n* **Topological Commit Graph Modal**: Monospace branch/merge lane visualization (`●"},{"id":"p21s6","text":"`, `◆`, `│`), commit links to Gitea Web UI, branch and tag badges, and live Gitea Actions CI statuse"},{"id":"p21s7","text":"s (`CI ✓`, `CI ✗`, `CI ●`).\n* **Cross-Tab Synchronization**: Efficient multi-tab coordination using "},{"id":"p21s8","text":"`navigator.locks` leader election and `BroadcastChannel`, eliminating duplicate network polling.\n* *"},{"id":"p21s9","text":"*Uncommitted Diff Inspector**: 1-click panel showing recent commits and uncommitted diff."},{"id":"p22s1","text":"### 3. Worktree Isolation & Agent Safety Rails"},{"id":"p23s1","text":"To allow autonomous agents to work on multiple issues without touching the primary branch:\n* **Non-d"},{"id":"p23s2","text":"estructive Worktrees**: Creates worktree paths under `.worktrees/issue-<id>/` or custom directories."},{"id":"p23s3","text":"\n* **Confirm Guard Matrix**: Destructive operations like `gitea_pr_merge` and `gitea_worktree_remove"},{"id":"p23s4","text":"` strictly require explicit boolean `confirm: true`. Unconfirmed tool calls are automatically reject"},{"id":"p23s5","text":"ed.\n* **Git Wrapper Enforcement**: Write operations can be routed through a dedicated wrapper (`gitW"},{"id":"p23s6","text":"rapper`, e.g., `git-deepseek-harness`) to enforce agent author signatures."}],"truncated":true}","role":"user"}],"model":"MiniMax-M3.1-Flash","reasoning_effort":"low","stream":false}
